  "summary": "Bakersfield Police credit Flock ALPR cameras with helping identify suspects in two child sex crime cases this month. The article also reviews the department's 58-camera network, its 30-day retention policy, California's SB 34 requirements, and broader national scrutiny of Flock.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Bakersfield police say automated license plate readers contributed to investigations into two alleged sex crimes involving children this month.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "The department maintains a policy of automatically deleting captured scan data after 30 days unless images are archived for an active criminal investigation.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Bakersfield police purchased 21 Flock cameras in 2021 before signing a three-year, $308,700 contract in 2023 to add 37 more units.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
